NebulaOS CAM-05 (2026-10-05): cache ustreamer's offline "blank" JPEG.

Upstream: pellcorp/ustreamer at 7fe8c87 (the k1-ustreamer submodule pinned
by K1_USTREAMER_PIN). Applied by scripts/build/04-cross-compile-app-stack.sh
to a copy of that exact tree with --fuzz=0; any context drift fails the build.
Recorded for later upstream submission; not submitted.

Problem: while the camera is paused (or absent) the stream's offline loop
calls us_blank_draw() every --device-error-delay second (1 s default). The
text render is already cached by us_frametext_draw(), but the 1080p RGB ->
JPEG q95 software encode ran every time: ~36 % of one X2000 CPU measured on
ke-dev, 2026-10-04 (0.7 % unpaused and idle).

Fix: us_blank_draw() re-encodes only when the text or size differs from what
blank->jpeg already holds (it keeps its own copy of the text; freed on change
and in us_blank_destroy()). Also leave the offline wait as soon as a paused
stream is resumed, instead of after the rest of the error delay. The live
(hardware-encoded MJPEG) path is not touched.

diff --git a/src/ustreamer/blank.c b/src/ustreamer/blank.c
index 09b1b00..7b57412 100644
--- a/src/ustreamer/blank.c
+++ b/src/ustreamer/blank.c
@@ -22,6 +22,9 @@
 
 #include "blank.h"
 
+#include <stdlib.h>
+#include <string.h>
+
 #include "../libs/types.h"
 #include "../libs/tools.h"
 #include "../libs/frame.h"
@@ -41,11 +44,28 @@ us_blank_s *us_blank_init(void) {
 }
 
 void us_blank_draw(us_blank_s *blank, const char *text, uint width, uint height) {
+	// The stream's offline loop redraws the blank every --device-error-delay
+	// (1 s by default) for as long as the camera is paused or absent, and the
+	// software JPEG encode below is the whole cost of that (frametext already
+	// skips an unchanged render). Encode only when the text or size changes;
+	// otherwise jpeg still holds exactly this blank.
+	if (
+		blank->jpeg_text != NULL && blank->jpeg->used > 0
+		&& blank->jpeg_width == width && blank->jpeg_height == height
+		&& !strcmp(blank->jpeg_text, text)
+	) {
+		return;
+	}
 	us_frametext_draw(blank->ft, text, width, height);
 	us_cpu_encoder_compress(blank->raw, blank->jpeg, 95);
+	US_DELETE(blank->jpeg_text, free);
+	blank->jpeg_text = us_strdup(text);
+	blank->jpeg_width = width;
+	blank->jpeg_height = height;
 }
 
 void us_blank_destroy(us_blank_s *blank) {
+	US_DELETE(blank->jpeg_text, free);
 	us_frame_destroy(blank->jpeg);
 	us_frametext_destroy(blank->ft);
 	free(blank);
diff --git a/src/ustreamer/blank.h b/src/ustreamer/blank.h
index 6e539e0..a8a4ff7 100644
--- a/src/ustreamer/blank.h
+++ b/src/ustreamer/blank.h
@@ -31,6 +31,10 @@ typedef struct {
 	us_frametext_s	*ft;
 	us_frame_s		*raw;
 	us_frame_s		*jpeg;
+	// What jpeg currently holds, so an unchanged blank is not re-encoded
+	char			*jpeg_text;
+	uint			jpeg_width;
+	uint			jpeg_height;
 } us_blank_s;
 
 
